<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ramchandra Pant Amatya</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1650">1650</a>–<a href="/years/1716">1716</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ramchandra Pant Amatya was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha</a> statesman who served <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shivaji">Shivaji</a> and his successors as a minister. During the war with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aurangzeb">Aurangzeb</a> in the 1690s, while Rajaram was besieged at Jinji, he directed the defence of the Maratha <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bantustan">homeland</a>. He wrote the Adnyapatra, a treatise on statecraft. His descendants held the hereditary title of Amatya and the estate of Bavda.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ramchandra-pant-amatya.jpg" alt="Ramchandra Pant Amatya" width="320" height="451" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Vedika201 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ramchandrapant_Amatya.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
